Z||000030||batboy||07-25-99||07:13 PM||||Speaking of trains and Fieros, this story was in the national news awhile back and FOCOA also published an article about it. A young lady in a Fiero was at a train crossing waiting for a train to go by and was hit from the rear by a van or truck which pushed her into and partly under the train. Her car was dragged for a few miles, I think, until it hit a pole or sign and was knocked loose. During this time she hunkered down inside the car and used her cell phone twice to call her mom and 911 for help. The train engineer didn't even know what had happened. She suffered only relatively minor injuries, but the picture I saw of that car was unbelievable. You'd of swore nobody could have lived through it. I guess these Fieros are built pretty tough.
